{
  "rules": [
    "Use The Composable Architecture (TCA) for state management. Structure each feature with State, Action, Reducer, and View files.",
    "Use Swift Concurrency (async/await) instead of Combine where possible.",
    "Favor structs and enums. Avoid classes unless necessary for UIKit or delegate patterns.",
    "Adopt SwiftUI best practices: computed properties for derived state, `@Dependency` for environment data, and minimal side effects in views.",
    "When accessing HealthKit, create a dedicated HealthKitManager service conforming to a protocol, with dependency injection.",
    "All code should be production-quality, cleanly formatted, and include concise explanatory comments for architecture choices.",
    "Use consistent naming: FeatureNameView, FeatureNameReducer, FeatureNameAction, etc.",
    "Generate TODOs when an API call or logic cannot be implemented without credentials or external data.",
    "Prefer clarity over brevity. Avoid over-abstracting too early.",
    "Follow Apple's Human Interface Guidelines for navigation and UX flow."
  ]
}
